-# Locals:
-#   problem    — a symbol from ConnectionsController
-#   connection — the connection being saved
-#   existing   — the other connection a duplicate matched, if any
-#
-# Each message says what happened and what to do next. Shown just after the
-# h1, and the fields point at it with aria-describedby. In the site's alert box
-# rather than .error-messages, so it can't be missed.
.flash.flash--alert.journal-notice#connection-problem{tabindex: "-1"}
  - case problem
  - when :already_connected
    %p
      You've already connected
      = succeed "." do
        %strong= existing.username
      To replace its key,
      = succeed "." do
        = link_to "manage #{existing.username}", journal_dw_connection_path(existing)
  - when :key_already_added
    %p
      You've already added this key: it's the one for
      = succeed "." do
        %strong= existing.username
      Dreamwidth gives each account its own key, so you were probably logged in to Dreamwidth as #{existing.username}.
      Log out of Dreamwidth, log in as #{connection.username}, then get the key again.
  - when :key_rejected
    %p Dreamwidth didn't accept that key. Check you copied all of it.
  - when :wrong_account
    %p
      That key belongs to a different Dreamwidth account than
      = succeed "." do
        %strong= connection.username
      Check which account you're logged in to on Dreamwidth, then get the key again.
  - when :no_such_journal
    %p
      Dreamwidth doesn't have an account called
      = succeed "." do
        %strong= connection.username
  - when :no_key
    %p Paste the new key first.
  - when :unavailable
    %p Couldn't reach Dreamwidth just now, so nothing was saved. Try again in a few minutes.
  - else
    - connection.errors.full_messages.each do |message|
      %p= message
